# Drive Character::AlignLawChaosProbe (src/Prayer.cpp) for bd inc-r6ae: does
# the law/chaos half of Character::AlignedAct ever set AL_LAWFUL/AL_CHAOTIC?
# Read by tools/check_align_lawchaos.sh.
#
# The probe fires once, from Game::Play() (src/Main.cpp), after the player and
# the map are live -- so this script only has to build a character and reach
# the dungeon. It starts as the same neutral orc barbarian tools/keys/chargen.keys
# makes everywhere; the probe resets the alignment stati to neutral itself, so
# the starting alignment is not what is under test.
#
# The probe logs one Error() line per case into logs/errors.log:
#   ALIGN_PROBE case=neutral-lawful-desired acts=5 alignLC=.. alignGE=..
#       align=0x.. lawful=. chaotic=. good=. evil=.
# Three law/chaos cases and three good/evil twin controls, both axes logged
# so tools/check_align_lawchaos.sh can compare like with like. Six only:
# Error() caps the distinct messages one session logs.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

s*3     # search, to run a few turns so the session is a real one
@dump:walked
@quit
